course: dictionary
lesson: 6412
title: Musician
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A musician is a person who plays a musical instrument or sings, often with great skill. A musician can also be a composer, someone who writes music. A violinist, a drummer, a pianist and a singer are all musicians.
explain: Being a musician takes lots of practice. Read the words around the word to check: «Playing a whole piece over and over repeats the same mistake; musicians stop at the tricky bar, play it slowly and correctly, then join it back in.» Here the musicians are the people who practise until they play well.
explain: Some musicians play by ear, which means they work out music by listening, not by reading the notes. Buskers are musicians too: they play in the street, often for money.
fact: A musician is a person who plays a musical instrument or sings.
fact: A composer is a musician who writes music.
fact: «A talented musician» is a musician who is very good at music, often without much effort.
fact: «Street musician» means a musician who plays in the street, often for money.
fact: Musicians often wear earplugs on stage: they make the sound quieter but still clear.
exercise: Lena plays the violin in the school orchestra. What is Lena? | *A musician | A painter | A baker
exercise: Which word means a musician who plays in the street for money? | *Busker | Composer | Conductor
exercise: «Musicians' earplugs make sound quieter but still clear.» What do the earplugs do? | Make sound louder and harsher | Stop all sound forever | Make the music play faster | *Make sound quieter but still clear
test: A composer is a musician who does what? | Sings only in the shower | *Writes music | Bakes bread | Paints pictures
test: Playing by ear means: | Stopping at the tricky bar | Reading every note on paper | Playing with your eyes closed | *Working out music by listening
exam: Which of these is NOT a musician? | Drummer | Pianist | *Painter | Violinist
